From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Manish Honap <mhonap@nvidia.com>
Date: Thu, 16 Jul 2026 22:27:09 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] NVIDIA: VR: SAUCE: vfio/cxl: borrow PCI Memory Space for
 post-reset BAR access

BugLink: https://bugs.launchpad.net/bugs/2163076

vfio_cxl_finish_reset() re-snapshots the emulated HDM decoder state by
reading the component register BAR. The reset path saves and restores PCI
config around the reset, so a guest that cleared PCI_COMMAND Memory Space
beforehand gets it back disabled and those reads are completed with an
Unsupported Request; on platforms that promote UR to a fatal error this
fires DPC.

Enable Memory Space for the snapshot and put the Command word back
afterwards, mirroring cxl_hdm_enable_mem() and cxl_hdm_restore_command()
in the CXL core. Leaving it enabled is not an option: only INTX_DISABLE is
virtualized, so the guest reads Memory Space from hardware while
__vfio_pci_memory_enabled() reads vfio's vconfig copy. A one-way enable
makes the two disagree, and every BAR access through vfio then fails with
-EIO or SIGBUS while the guest believes its BARs are live.

Bail out without snapshotting if Memory Space cannot be turned on, rather
than reading all ones and re-arming the DPA region off a COMMITTED bit that
came from a floating bus.

memory_lock is held for writing here, so BAR fd I/O, the fault path and
guest Command writes are all excluded for the duration. A guest config read
of PCI_COMMAND is not serialized against this and can observe Memory Space
set for the length of the snapshot.

Signed-off-by: Manish Honap <mhonap@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Jiandi An <jan@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Seth Forshee <sforshee@nvidia.com>
Acked-by: Matthew R. Ochs <mochs@nvidia.com>
Signed-off-by: Brad Figg <bfigg@nvidia.com>
Ledger-Change: C-01908
Ledger-Origin: nvidia-bos@80f3b2774f5b36f0a29c13c7e89963003a11d573
---
 drivers/vfio/pci/cxl/vfio_cxl_core.c | 47 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 47 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/vfio/pci/cxl/vfio_cxl_core.c b/drivers/vfio/pci/cxl/vfio_cxl_core.c
index 61f85495d412..4c0fcb483ea9 100644
--- a/drivers/vfio/pci/cxl/vfio_cxl_core.c
+++ b/drivers/vfio/pci/cxl/vfio_cxl_core.c
@@ -793,6 +793,43 @@ void vfio_cxl_prepare_reset(struct vfio_pci_core_device *vdev)
 	vfio_cxl_zap_dpa(vdev);
 }
 
+/*
+ * vfio_cxl_borrow_memory_space - turn Memory Space on for the component
+ * register reads, reporting whether it has to be put back.
+ *
+ * The reset path saves and restores PCI config around the reset, so a guest
+ * that cleared PCI_COMMAND Memory Space beforehand gets it back disabled.
+ * Reading a BAR in that state produces an Unsupported Request completion;
+ * on platforms that promote UR to a fatal error this fires DPC.
+ *
+ * Borrow it rather than keep it: vfio tracks Memory Space in vconfig while
+ * the guest reads it from hardware, so leaving it enabled would make
+ * __vfio_pci_memory_enabled() disagree with what the guest sees.  Mirrors
+ * cxl_hdm_enable_mem().
+ */
+static int vfio_cxl_borrow_memory_space(struct vfio_pci_core_device *vdev,
+					u16 *cmd, bool *restore)
+{
+	int rc;
+
+	*restore = false;
+
+	rc = pci_read_config_word(vdev->pdev, PCI_COMMAND, cmd);
+	if (rc)
+		return pcibios_err_to_errno(rc);
+
+	if (*cmd & PCI_COMMAND_MEMORY)
+		return 0;
+
+	rc = pci_write_config_word(vdev->pdev, PCI_COMMAND,
+				   *cmd | PCI_COMMAND_MEMORY);
+	if (rc)
+		return pcibios_err_to_errno(rc);
+
+	*restore = true;
+	return 0;
+}
+
 /*
  * vfio_cxl_finish_reset - Re-enable DPA region after reset.
  *
@@ -803,11 +840,18 @@ void vfio_cxl_prepare_reset(struct vfio_pci_core_device *vdev)
 void vfio_cxl_finish_reset(struct vfio_pci_core_device *vdev)
 {
 	struct vfio_pci_cxl_state *cxl = vdev->cxl;
+	bool restore_command;
+	u16 command;
 
 	lockdep_assert_held_write(&vdev->memory_lock);
 
 	if (!cxl)
 		return;
+
+	/* Without Memory Space the snapshot below reads all ones. */
+	if (vfio_cxl_borrow_memory_space(vdev, &command, &restore_command))
+		return;
+
 	/*
 	 * Re-initialise the emulated HDM comp_reg_virt[] from hardware.
 	 * A reset clears decoder registers; mirror that in the emulated
@@ -815,6 +859,9 @@ void vfio_cxl_finish_reset(struct vfio_pci_core_device *vdev)
 	 */
 	vfio_cxl_reinit_comp_regs(cxl);
 
+	if (restore_command)
+		pci_write_config_word(vdev->pdev, PCI_COMMAND, command);
+
 	/*
 	 * Only re-enable the DPA mmap if the hardware has actually
 	 * re-committed decoder 0 after FLR.  Read the COMMITTED bit from the
